  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CARDSW-Enhance Access to education</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ultimate goal of the project is to increase legal awareness and understanding on the rights to access education and safety and security of inland waterways amongst children of ethnic minorities and their parents who go to school by boat, in Hoa Binh province.Project activities are designed to disseminate Constitution 2013 and Law on Inland Waterway Traffic 2014, using 2 approaches of school-based and needs-based. The focus groups are students, parents and teachers in 3 primary and secondary schools.Legal aid, communication and training activities at schools will be organized or curriculum-integrated and tailored concerning the focus group&#x2019; abilities and needs. Moreover, there will be communications campaigns on drowning prevention launched, and on-campus drowning prevention consulting centers established to spread the project impacts. Last but not least, the initiative proposes contributions to developingpolicies and laws related to students of ethnic minorities in river regions. At the end of theproject, it is expected to help increase awareness on children&#x2019;s rights to access education issued in Constitution 13 and Law on Inland Waterway Traffic 2014 for 80% teachers and 90% parents of students studying at 3 piloted schools who go to school by boat. Events organized at schools, additionally,aim to attract about 780 students while the model of on-campus drowning prevention consulting centers at 3 schools would record up to 540 students&#x2019; visits from 11/2023 to 4/2024.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="90">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Center for Applied Research and</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Center for Applied Research and Development of Social Work (CARDSW) is a member of Faculty of Sociology, University of Social Sciences and Humanities, Vietnamese National University, Hanoi
- 2005, Participated with the Ministry of Labour, Invalids and Social Affairs to develop the &quot;Law on Gender Equality&quot;- 2006-2011: Participated in the &quot;Rural Water Supply and Sanitation Project in the Red River Delta of Vietnam (RRDRWSS) in Nam Dinh&quot;, International Development Association (IDA), World Bank- In 2012-2013, Co-chair of the project &quot;The status of understanding and main sources of access to the Law on Gender Equality of ethnic minority women in Yen Son District, Tuyen Quang Province&quot; funded by the Jiff Foundation - In 2013-2014, the Organization mobilized the participation of ethnic minority communities in contributing to the development of the Law on Supervision activities of the People&apos;s Council and improving the accountability of the authorities in the district. Yen Lap, Phu Tho province.- In 2016-2019, Strengthen the participation of people with disabilities, social organizations and people in supervising the implementation of the Law on Education and related policies for people with disabilities in Cam Xuyen district, province Ha Tinh.- 2011-2013: Trained as a trainer for staff of the Protection Department of 63 provinces and cities on &quot;Environmental protection in social protection establishments&quot; organized by the Department of Protection- 2015, Organizing training for students of the Faculty of Sociology on the Law on Environmental Protection 2014; In2018 - 2020, Join with the Ministry of Labour, Invalids and Social Affairs to develop the &quot;Law on Social Work&quot;. In 2018, Participated with the Ministry of Natural Resources and Environment Workshop on adjusting and amending &quot;Law on environmental protection in 2020&quot;</narrative>
  </participating-org>
